  "has_quantitative_results": true,
  "summary": "The paper simulates a deep quantum neural network (DQNN) with 4–5 qubits to learn financial quantities. In a 7‑sample implied volatility task it achieves fidelity up to C = 0.9999 with volatility errors of a few basis points, and in a Black–Scholes experiment it predicts option prices, deltas, and gammas from 7 training samples using a 5‑qubit simulated network. All results are obtained via MATLAB simulation with no hardware execution or classical baseline comparison.",
